# Generated screencasts and their build artifacts are not committed, only the
# scripts that produce them. record.sh writes all of this into the permission's
# own folder so the videos live next to the declaration they belong to, but they
# stay local: they are large, regenerable, and what gets submitted to Google is a
# hosted URL rather than a file from here.
*.mp4
captions.txt
title.txt
end.txt
ui.xml
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
